  "problem": "A particular town has a fleet of $720$ bicycles for rent. The table below gives the pattern of rental and return locations over a typical day. \n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td colspan=\"3\" align=\"center\">From:</td> \n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td width=\"60\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Museum</b></td>\n<td width=\"60\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Station</b></td> \n<td width=\"60\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Gym</b></td> \n</tr>\n<tr> \n<td rowspan=\"3\" align=\"center\">To:</td>\n<td width=\"60\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Museum</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.9$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n<td width=\"60\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Station</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.7$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n<td width=\"60\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Gym</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nFor example, $40%$ of the bicycles at the Station are moved to the Gym every day.\n\nHow many bicycles would eventually be located at the Station if the listed probabilities remained constant over many days?",
